# --- Unavailable tracks + replacement search (Qt port, contract 2026-08-17
# §8-6). "Unavailable" and "This track is no longer available" already
# exist in this file and are REUSED by the render and the reactive skip toast
# — nothing below twins them.
#
# The skipped-tracks toast is a plural PAIR, per the convention already set by
# "Scan complete ({} file skipped)" and "{} duplicate skipped": the queue build
# drops N rows at once, and a singular-only string reads wrong in every locale
# with plural rules. Russian carries all three forms.
#
# "No longer on Qobuz — playing your downloaded copy" is the cached-but-pulled
# state (contract §5.3/F5): the track left the catalogue but the user owns a
# downloaded copy, so it still plays. It cannot fold into "This track is no
# longer available" — that sentence would be a lie on a row playing right now.
#
# Em dash is U+2014 with spaces on both sides, as everywhere else in this file.
# en is the source-language stub: msgstr == msgid, as every batch that
# introduced a genuinely new msgid here has done.
