#: qbz-qt/qml/settings/PlaybackSettings.qml
msgid "Playback memory preset conflicts with custom cache limits"
msgstr "Playback memory preset conflicts with custom cache limits"

msgid "Apply playback memory profile?"
msgstr "Apply playback memory profile?"

msgid "Playback buffers will be released. If playing, the current track will stop and restart from the beginning. If paused, it will stay stopped at 0:00. Your queue and disk cache will be kept."
msgstr "Playback buffers will be released. If playing, the current track will stop and restart from the beginning. If paused, it will stay stopped at 0:00. Your queue and disk cache will be kept."

msgid "Apply & free memory"
msgstr "Apply & free memory"

msgid "Rebuild playback buffers"
msgstr "Rebuild playback buffers"

msgid "The profile already applies to new buffers. Apply now to release existing playback buffers and the memory cache. Memory use can grow again as playback continues."
msgstr "The profile already applies to new buffers. Apply now to release existing playback buffers and the memory cache. Memory use can grow again as playback continues."

msgid "Playback memory can only be applied to local playback."
msgstr "Playback memory can only be applied to local playback."

msgid "Playback is not ready yet."
msgstr "Playback is not ready yet."

msgid "Playback is busy. Try applying the memory profile again."
msgstr "Playback is busy. Try applying the memory profile again."

msgid "Playback changed. Apply again to confirm the current track."
msgstr "Playback changed. Apply again to confirm the current track."

msgid "Visual resource profile"
msgstr "Visual resource profile"

msgid "Low uses the Small player, compact headers, no dynamic background, header gradient, spectrum, animated play indicator, sidebar collages or optional track artwork. Default restores these visual defaults. Editing a managed option selects Custom. Audio quality and playback memory are independent."
msgstr "Low uses the Small player, compact headers, no dynamic background, header gradient, spectrum, animated play indicator, sidebar collages or optional track artwork. Default restores these visual defaults. Editing a managed option selects Custom. Audio quality and playback memory are independent."

msgid "Compare memory profiles"
msgstr "Compare memory profiles"

msgid "Auto: fixed 400 MiB or 50 MiB according to the computer's RAM; disk handles larger tracks."
msgstr "Auto: fixed 400 MiB or 50 MiB according to the computer's RAM; disk handles larger tracks."

msgid "High: dynamic 400–1600 MiB; more room in RAM for large tracks, with less need for disk-backed buffers."
msgstr "High: dynamic 400–1600 MiB; more room in RAM for large tracks, with less need for disk-backed buffers."

msgid "Desktop: fixed 400 MiB; balances RAM use with disk-backed playback for larger tracks."
msgstr "Desktop: fixed 400 MiB; balances RAM use with disk-backed playback for larger tracks."

msgid "Low: fixed 50 MiB and reduced prefetch; lower RAM use, with more disk reads and writes for large tracks."
msgstr "Low: fixed 50 MiB and reduced prefetch; lower RAM use, with more disk reads and writes for large tracks."

msgid "Custom: your RAM limits and growth preference determine when playback needs disk storage."
msgstr "Custom: your RAM limits and growth preference determine when playback needs disk storage."

msgid "RAM and storage trade-off"
msgstr "RAM and storage trade-off"

msgid "All profiles preserve audio quality and can use disk cache. Lower memory budgets rely more on storage speed and writes; more RAM can reduce that work. Cached disk tracks are read from disk even in High. Choose storage appropriate for your listening workload."
msgstr "All profiles preserve audio quality and can use disk cache. Lower memory budgets rely more on storage speed and writes; more RAM can reduce that work. Cached disk tracks are read from disk even in High. Choose storage appropriate for your listening workload."

msgid "Playback storage folder"
msgstr "Playback storage folder"

msgid "Choose an existing folder on the drive you want to use. QBZ stores its playback cache and temporary track buffers in a qbz-playback subfolder. Offline downloads are separate. Leave blank for the default location."
msgstr "Choose an existing folder on the drive you want to use. QBZ stores its playback cache and temporary track buffers in a qbz-playback subfolder. Offline downloads are separate. Leave blank for the default location."

msgid "Current playback storage"
msgstr "Current playback storage"

msgid "Changing the folder takes effect after restarting QBZ. Existing cache files stay in the old location; they are not moved or deleted automatically."
msgstr "Changing the folder takes effect after restarting QBZ. Existing cache files stay in the old location; they are not moved or deleted automatically."

msgid "Could not use this playback storage folder:"
msgstr "Could not use this playback storage folder:"

msgid "Folder access"
msgstr "Folder access"

msgid "If the sandbox blocks this folder, run the command below in a host terminal, restart QBZ, then select the folder again. Only grant access to a folder you intend to use."
msgstr "If the sandbox blocks this folder, run the command below in a host terminal, restart QBZ, then select the folder again. Only grant access to a folder you intend to use."

msgid "Snap can access supported home folders and removable storage under /mnt, /media or /run/media. For removable storage, connect the interface below and retry. Snap cannot grant arbitrary folder access with a Flatpak-style override."
msgstr "Snap can access supported home folders and removable storage under /mnt, /media or /run/media. For removable storage, connect the interface below and retry. Snap cannot grant arbitrary folder access with a Flatpak-style override."

msgid "Choose an absolute folder path for playback storage."
msgstr "Choose an absolute folder path for playback storage."

msgid "The folder is accessible and visible in the library."
msgstr "The folder is accessible and visible in the library."

msgid "The folder is accessible but hidden by your preference."
msgstr "The folder is accessible but hidden by your preference."

msgid "The folder path no longer exists. Reconnect it, change its path or remove it from the library."
msgstr "The folder path no longer exists. Reconnect it, change its path or remove it from the library."

msgid "A connection failure prevents access to this storage."
msgstr "A connection failure prevents access to this storage."

msgid "QBZ does not have permission to access this folder."
msgstr "QBZ does not have permission to access this folder."

msgid "The folder could not be accessed. The check timed out or returned another access error."
msgstr "The folder could not be accessed. The check timed out or returned another access error."

msgid "Folder access is being checked or has not been checked yet."
msgstr "Folder access is being checked or has not been checked yet."

msgid "Local folder"
msgstr "Local folder"

msgid "Network folder"
msgstr "Network folder"

msgid "Access denied"
msgstr "Access denied"

msgid "Missing"
msgstr "Missing"

msgid "Disconnected"
msgstr "Disconnected"

msgid "Hidden"
msgstr "Hidden"

msgid "Active"
msgstr "Active"

